fix: safer API-route syntax, npm as primary tooling, Windows 10 docs, .gitattributes

- The 3 raw-HTTP routes (checkout, paddle-webhook, cron/retry-stuck-jobs)
  previously imported createServerFileRoute from a subpath. If that export
  doesn't exist in the installed TanStack Start version, importing it is a
  hard module-resolution error that fails the ENTIRE build, not just these
  routes — this is a plausible second contributor to the 'endless errors'
  reported after the Vercel/Netlify attempts, on top of the Cloudflare
  target. Rewritten using createFileRoute (proven correct — every other
  route in this project already uses it successfully) with a
  server.handlers option instead. If that option shape is also wrong for
  the installed version, the failure mode is now isolated to these 3
  endpoints (typecheck flags it, or the route just 404s) instead of blocking
  the whole app.
- npm is now the documented primary package manager (no code changes needed
  for this — confirmed zero Bun-specific runtime APIs anywhere in the app;
  Bun was only ever used as an install tool). bunfig.toml is left in place
  for anyone who still wants to use Bun, but every instruction now leads
  with npm, which needs no separate installer on Windows.
- README rewritten end to end for a Windows 10 user who is not a programmer:
  exact PowerShell steps for install/env/Supabase CLI/run/build/deploy,
  plus a troubleshooting section. Added a 'start' script matching Nitro's
  standard node-server output path, documented as unverified against a
  real build.
- .gitattributes: normalize line endings so Windows contributors don't get
  spurious CRLF/LF diffs.
- Diagnostic pass with noUnusedLocals/noUnusedParameters temporarily
  enabled in the verification harness (not the project's own tsconfig) ->
  zero findings anywhere, including generated UI primitives.
- Searched the whole src/ tree for TODO/FIXME/placeholder/mock/dummy/fake
  markers -> zero real matches (every hit was a legitimate Tailwind
  placeholder: class or an i18n *Placeholder input-hint key).
- Confirmed no duplicate implementations: exactly 4 createClient call
  sites, each for a genuinely distinct purpose (persistent browser client,
  persistent admin client, two request-scoped clients for user-token vs.
  anonymous access) — not redundant. Mapped the .server.ts import graph:
  acyclic, no circular dependencies.
- Confirmed getLesson never calls AI — lessons are generated once during
  processing and only ever read afterward, never regenerated on page view.

Verified: real-tsc harness -> 0 errors. Import checker -> 0 broken imports
(484 specifiers, 108 files).
